# Line endings, pinned.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The «Архив» redesign branch committed src/index.css
# with CRLF into a repository that stores LF, and the result was a diff of
# 2568 insertions against 2070 deletions for a file where a few hundred lines
# had actually changed — every untouched line rewritten because its invisible
# terminator differed. `git diff --check` reported 5136 whitespace errors, and
# review, `git blame` and any later merge all inherited the noise.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is a per-developer setting and cannot be relied on: it is a
# property of whoever happens to clone next. This file makes the answer a
# property of the REPOSITORY, which is where it belongs.
#
# LF in the object database, always. Windows editors handle LF fine; the
# working tree may be converted by autocrlf locally, and that is nobody else's
# business because it never reaches a commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched, never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
